  - Share, resell, generate or guess activation codes, or get around the
    licence checks, the Pro features or the limit on computers.
  - Remove or change the copyright notices, the creator's name or the
    signatures of the app.
  - Use the source code, where you have been given access to it (for example
    a private repository), for anything other than building and running Swep
    for the creator.

Third-party software
  Swep bundles and uses components under their own licences, which keep
  their own terms and are not changed by this licence: the cleaning runtime
  it ships (GNU GPL version 3 - its licence and notice travel with it and are
  shown under About -> Licence), the Tauri framework and the Rust and
  JavaScript libraries it is built from, and the system tools it runs.

Updates and the licence server
  Swep checks for updates, and checks activation codes and subscriptions
  with the creator's server. Those checks send only what they need: the code
  or subscription id, an anonymous machine id, the app version and the
  operating system. Once a day Swep also counts itself as an installed copy
  with the same anonymous details; Settings -> "Tell the creator Swep is in
  use" turns that off. Nothing from your files leaves your computer.

No warranty
  Swep is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind. It removes only
  what you confirm, and it keeps what it can in the Trash or Put Back; even
  so, to the extent the law allows, the creator is not liable for data loss
  or any other damage arising from its use. Keep a backup.

Ending this licence
  This licence ends if you break its terms. When it ends, stop using Swep and
  delete your copies. Clauses that by their nature outlast it (the ownership
  of the work, the no-warranty clause) remain.

